{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc | sed -n '820,890p;1060,1165p;1230,1365p;1490,1640p'; rg -n 'tail|capture|continuation' src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc | head -60\"","aggregated_output":"   820\t  [env sym]\n   821\t  (when-let [conv (::convention env)]\n   822\t    (and (symbol? sym)\n   823\t         (not (contains? (locals env) sym))\n   824\t         (not (contains? (::defined env) sym))\n   825\t         (or (some? (namespace sym))\n   826\t             (contains? (:native conv) sym)))))\n   827\t\n   828\t\n   829\t(defn- macro-call?\n   830\t  [env macro-env sym]\n   831\t  (and (symbol? sym)\n   832\t       (not (contains? (locals env) sym))\n   833\t       (or (contains? macro-env sym)\n   834\t           (contains? (:macros (::convention env)) sym))))\n   835\t\n   836\t\n   837\t;; =============================================================================\n   838\t;; Outcome model (slice 5)\n   839\t;; =============================================================================\n   840\t;;\n   841\t;; Opted in with `:outcomes true` beside the argument-vector convention. Every\n   842\t;; guest function then returns an outcome, a tagged two-element vector:\n   843\t;;\n   844\t;;   [:yin.k/ok value]       success; a LaTTe [:ok ...] stays an ordinary value\n   845\t;;   [:yin.k/error data]     failure; never a truthy return, only ever consumed\n   846\t;;                           by a call-site test or the harness boundary\n   847\t;;\n   848\t;; Lowering is a source-to-source pass over one function body, run before the\n   849\t;; ordinary compile. A tail form returns an outcome: a value is wrapped,\n   850\t;; and a source call is admitted before invoking the common entry. Generated\n   851\t;; entries can forward a private body's outcome directly in tail position;\n   852\t;; public entries convert value/raise through the caller bridge. This keeps\n   853\t;; named and mutual tail chains at constant depth. `throw` becomes the error\n   854\t;; outcome. A may-fail form in operand position is the early return pattern:\n   855\t;;\n   856\t;;   (let [o <outcome>] (if (error? o) o <rest of the function with (payload o)>))\n   857\t;;\n   858\t;; The failing branch returns the outcome in tail position. `ex-info` becomes\n   859\t;; a portable map under namespaced keys. A native primitive returns a raw\n   860\t;; value, except an adapted one (`:adapters`, source symbol to adapter symbol),\n   861\t;; whose host adapter already returns an outcome. Generated names carry the\n   862\t;; reserved `dsg__` prefix and bind through the internal `dsg__let`, which\n   863\t;; skips the user-binder check; the program pre-pass keeps user code out of\n   864\t;; that prefix. A macro call is opaque to the pass: the expander owns it.\n   865\t\n   866\t(def ^:private ok-tag :yin.k/ok)\n   867\t\n   868\t(def ^:private error-tag :yin.k/error)\n   869\t\n   870\t\n   871\t(defn- outcomes?\n   872\t  [env]\n   873\t  (some? (::outcomes env)))\n   874\t\n   875\t\n   876\t(defn- adapters\n   877\t  [env]\n   878\t  (:adapters (::outcomes env)))\n   879\t\n   880\t\n   881\t(defn- binder-symbols\n   882\t  [b]\n   883\t  (into #{} (comp (filter symbol?) (remove #{'&})) (tree-seq coll? seq b)))\n   884\t\n   885\t\n   886\t(defn- ok-form\n   887\t  [v]\n   888\t  [ok-tag v])\n   889\t\n   890\t\n  1060\t                  :else (go more (conj acc f))))))]\n  1061\t    (go (seq forms) [])))\n  1062\t\n  1063\t\n  1064\t(defn- lower-let\n  1065\t  \"`pairs` are plain [symbol init] pairs.\"\n  1066\t  [env pairs body]\n  1067\t  (letfn [(go\n  1068\t            [env ps]\n  1069\t            (if (empty? ps)\n  1070\t              (lower-tail env (body-expression body))\n  1071\t              (let [[x init] (first ps)]\n  1072\t                (lower-operand env init\n  1073\t                               (fn [v]\n  1074\t                    