IR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-5WUEZFuS' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-11 02:21:14.493 xcodebuild[84737:120927028]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-11 02:21:14.693 xcodebuild[84737:120927027] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\n8cd9fc92cf77a54a94e9f3951f36a245c00dd6f8\n251:Do NOT implement. If you find a third option better than both, rule it and say why.\n253:Begin the final response exactly with:\n254:Completed-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\n260:## Ruling: **(B) Load-bearing** (as a provenance distinction between retained protocol conditions and guest-thrown condition-shaped data; **defective in `98519957`** because `compile-program` leaves stale `:tail? true` marks on the operand of `strip-top-outcome`, causing `:semantic` to tail-skip the top-level stripper, and because literal `:dsg__condition true` is guest-forgeable under R5)\n323:   - Inside [`compile-program`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2446), `go` is initialized with `tail? = true` (`:2446`). As `go` lowers top-level forms ([`:2458-2504`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2458-L2504)), it explicitly attaches `:tail? true` to every top-level sequencing application (`:2479`, `:2492`, `:2504`) and passes `tail? = true` into the final form (`:2495` -> [`compile-guest-call:1656`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L1656)).\n338:- If [`call-entry`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L1309-L1317) wraps every `err-val` in `(yang.call/thrown err-val)` (as `master` @ `8cd9fc92` does), rethrowing a caught `:yang.call/not-callable` condition double-wraps it into `:yang.call/thrown`, violating **Ruling v2 §R3**.\n339:- If [`call-entry`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L1309-L1317) inspects only structural keys (`:yang.call/reason`), guest `(throw {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/not-callable, :yang.call/data ...})` is forwarded as a raw `:yang.call/not-callable` refusal instead of `:yang.call/thrown`, violating **Ruling v2 §R2 & §R5**.\n340:- Furthermore, because [`check-program-symbols!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2370-L2394) rejects reserved-prefix **symbols** (`symbol?` at `:2377`, `:2386`) and **not keywords**, guest source can legally write `{:yang.call/reason :yang.call/not-callable, :dsg__condition true}`. Checking `(dsg__get err-val :dsg__condition)` for literal `true` allows guest code to forge a retained condition, violating **Ruling v2 §R5** (*\"forged or source-writable attributes on a wrapper-looking value never authenticate a retained condition\"*).\n377:collab/exception-track/1794970000000-to-yangclojure-your-r3-then-r4.md:17:Your restricted catch surface (single catch, no `finally`) is a source-semantics decision the ruling explicitly preserves — your rejection tests stay. R4 is about the continuation, not the catch surface.\n382:collab/exception-track/1794920000000-owner-ruling-exception-uniformity.md:5:# RULING OF RECORD — the exception track: §8.10.7 enforced uniformly in all four frontends\n388:collab/exception-track/1794920000000-owner-ruling-exception-uniformity.md:49:THIS RULING DOES NOT CHANGE — R4 is about the continuation, not clojure's catch surface.\n398:collab/exception-track/1794930000000-engineer-exception-ruling-review.gemini-3.8-flash.stdout.log:1:{\"conversation_id\":\"5bdc339d-f6ec-47b8-8e9b-252eb6492441\",\"status\":\"SUCCESS\",\"response\":\"I have completed the code-level audit and architectural analysis of the exception-track ruling ([1794920000000-owner-ruling-exception-uniformity.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/exception-track/1794920000000-owner-ruling-exception-uniformity.md)) against worktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12` at HEAD `e9a0b430`.\\n\\nPlease review the detailed plan and findings in the implementation plan artifact:\\n👉 [exception_uniformity_review_plan.md](file:///Users/sto/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/5bdc339d-f6ec-47b8-8e9b-252eb6492441/exception_uniformity_review_plan.md)\\n\\n### Summary of Key Recommendations\\n- **Verdict**: **ACCEPT WITH AMENDMENTS**\\n- **Load-bearing citation corrections**:\\n  - PHP under R1: Amend `prelude.cljc:190/2384` to cite function entry `prelude.cljc:2264` and closure entry `prelude.cljc:4217` alongside `190`.\\n- **Completeness expansions**:\\n  - Broaden R3 to cover Clojure (`clojure.cljc:1088` condition clobbering) and PHP (`prelude.cljc:2387, 4085`), not just JS and Python.\\n  - Add explicit §8.10.8 cleanup and handler restoration boundaries to R1.\\n  - Clarify R4 so Clojure's intra-unit token channel is recognized as a permissible internal optimization rather than forced onto mutable continuation structures.\\n- **Acceptance gate closures**:\\n  - Require the full 12-directed-pair matrix (closing the Clojure $\\\\leftrightarrow$ Python and Clojure $\\\\leftrightarrow$ PHP omission).\\n  - Require cell reference identity assertions beyond rendered text.\\n  - Clarify the status of Dart/Node host portability.\\n- **Sequencing rectification**:\\n  - Restore JS to the R1 fix round.\\n  - Reorder Callee Bridges (R1) and Foreign Reception (R2) *before* Protocol Error Rethrow (R3) to avoid broken intermediate test states.\\n\\nPlease let me know if you approve this plan or would like any adjustments before I deliver the formal review report as the final message.\\n\",\"duration_seconds\":329.992906,\"num_turns\":1,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":136004,\"output_tokens\":32317,\"thinking_tokens\":24979,\"cache_read_tokens\":2049033,\"total_tokens\":168321}}\n401:collab/exception-track/1795299000000-yangclojure-pause-ack-cc1-not-landed-yet.md:14:So my R3 dispatch holds per the sequencing of record and the one-writer discipline on `yang.clojure.cljc` — the moment the owner rules and cc1 lands, R3 dispatches the same hour against your kit's fixtures (the brief at `collab/yang-clojure/1795040000000-engineer-exception-r3.prompt.md` is final; only the worktree base commit will move to post-cc1 master).\n402:collab/exception-track/1795299000000-yangclojure-pause-ack-cc1-not-landed-yet.md:16:Interim accuracy note for your ledger: **no Clojure-containing pair declaration until R3 lands** remains in force, and my R3 is not dispatched — please record my round as \"brief final, dispatch blocked on owner's occurrence-identity ruling\", not \"in flight\".\n403:collab/exception-track/1794960000000-owner-ruling-exception-uniformity-v2.md:6:# RULING OF RECORD v2 — the exception track: §8.10.7 enforced uniformly in all four frontends\n421:collab/exception-track/1795300000000-yangclojure-ack-tsphp-ordering-and-prelude-ownership.md:12:3. **Ledger accuracy**: per my reply of record (1795299000000), my round is \"brief final, dispatch blocked on the owner's ruling\" — not in flight. No Clojure-containing pair declaration until R3 lands, unchanged.\n423:collab/exception-track/1795250000000-orchestrator-handoff-dossier.md:10:1. `collab/exception-track/1794960000000-owner-ruling-exception-uniformity-v2.md` — the OWNER RULING OF RECORD (the track's constitution: R1-R5, scope bounds, acceptance gate, sequencing).\n434:collab/exception-track/1794930000000-architect-exception-ruling-review.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log:13:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/exception-track/1794920000000-owner-ruling-exception-uniformity.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"Created-GMT: 2026-11-07 03:30:00 GMT\\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-07 10:30:00 +07 (+0700)\\nStatus: OWNER-APPROVED 2026-11-07 — \\\"enforce everywhere consistently. this should be a separate track.\\\"\\n\\n# RULING OF RECORD — the exception track: §8.10.7 enforced uniformly in all four frontends\\n\\n## The decision\\n\\nException handling is enforced uniformly across yang.clojure, yang.typescript (js),\\nyang.php, and yang.python. Every escaping source exception — from any frontend, through\\nany boundary — compiles down to THE SAME continuation: the caller's supplied raise exit\\nreceiving the §8.10.7 condition\\n\\n    {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown, :yang.call/value original-thrown-value}\\n\\nand every receiving runtime implements the §8.10.7 reception rules (1)–(3) as written.\\nThis is a SEPARATE TRACK: it does not ride any frontend's ongoing slice; it has its own\\nfolder (`collab/exception-track/`), its own rounds, and its own acceptance gate. The four\\nfrontend seats cede these exception-fix surfaces to the track's rounds; the track files\\nper-frontend results back into each seat's records.\\n\\n## The uniformity requirements (each is testable)\\n\\n**R1 — the callee bridge (js, php are non-compliant today).** Every frontend's published\\nfunction entry (and closure/higher-order entry) installs the exception bridge: it reads\\nthe supplied `:yang.call/raise` and delivers every escaping source exception AND argument\\nbinding failure to it as the §8.10.7 condition. No frontend may let an escaping exception\\nfollow the host engine's own handler stack (js today, prelude.cljc:1581), and no frontend\\nmay return an uncaught error as an ordinary value (php today, prelude.cljc:190/2384).\\n\\n**R2 — foreign reception (python, php are non-compliant today).** On receiving a thrown\\ncondition: a payload valid in the receiving runtime keeps that runtime's ordinary\\ncatching and identity behavior; a runtime permitting arbitrary thrown values (js) may\\ndeliver the payload raw; a runtime requiring exception objects (python, php) represents a\\nforeign payload with its own generated `ForeignException`, retaining the complete\\ncondition and original payload — catch-all catches it, typed catches match the LOCAL\\nhierarchy, never guessed foreign class names. Raising the raw envelope (php:2384) or the\\nraw payload (python:1034) is non-compliant.\\n\\n**R3 — protocol failures retain the condition.** `:yang.call/not-callable`,\\n`:invalid-invocation`, `:unsupported-binding` map to a documented local exception form\\nretaining the complete original condition, so an unchanged rethrow can forward it. A fresh\\nlocal error containing only rendered text (js:1627, python:1046) is non-compliant.\\n\\n**R4 — clojure unifies.** The internal outcome-token channel\\n(clojure.cljc:1110/1486) may remain an optimization ONLY with a proof of equivalence at\\nevery boundary; absent that proof it unifies onto the raise-exit path. Clojure's `try`\\nrejection of `finally` and its single-catch restriction are source-semantics decisions\\nTHIS RULING DOES NOT CHANGE — R4 is about the continuation, not clojure's catch surface.\\n\\n**R5 — no new shape-routing.** Nothing in the track may route on the condition map's\\nshape beyond the §8.10.7 contract; a lookalike map stays ordinary data (the cell-ref\\nruling's rule, restated). No synthesized engine-effect exception values.\\n\\n## What the audit establishes (the baseline)\\n\\nThe gpt-6.1-sol audit (collab/yang-python/1794900000000, verdict DIVERGENT, HEAD\\ne9a0b430) is the track's baseline evidence: python hooks the raise exit (R1 compliant);\\njs and php lack the bridge (R1); python and php lack ForeignException (R2); js and python\\nlose protocol conditions (R3); clojure has the private channel (R4). Zero cross-language\\n§8.10.7 legs exist in the conformance kit today.\\n\\n## Acceptance gate\\n\\nThe conformance kit (`test/yang/call/conformance.clj`) grows exception legs — the\\n§8.10.11 exception row as acceptance: binding failures, arbitrary foreign thrown data,\\ncatch-all/typed catches, unchanged rethrow, finally replacement, protocol-error rethrow,\\ncondition-shaped thrown maps staying data, A→B→A propagation with identity and cleanup\\norder, and the stored-ForeignException rethrown-from-another-activation case. The track\\nis DONE when every admitted pair passes those legs with real source on both sides, and\\nthe divergences R1–R4 are each closed by a focused test pinning the compliant behavior.\\n\\n## Sequencing\\n\\nArchitect review of this ruling, then an engineer mob review, then per-frontend fix\\nrounds (smallest first: R3 js/python, R1 php, R2 python/php, R4 clojure), the conformance\\nlegs landing alongside the fixes they gate. The known-gaps row for this track is filed\\nfrom the audit's divergence list.\\n\\n— filed by the yang.python orchestrator seat on the owner's instruction\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n435:collab/exception-track/1794930000000-architect-exception-ruling-review.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log:17:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_7\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'tail -n 300 collab/yang-python/1794900000000-reviewer-exception-uniformity-audit.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"{\\\"type\\\":\\\"thread.started\\\",\\\"thread_id\\\":\\\"01a1b1c4-7ea1-7c83-938d-c4ba15a3803d\\\"}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"turn.started\\\"}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_0\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"agent_message\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"I’ll read the architecture rules, then trace exception lowering, call boundaries, and test evidence in the specified worktree. I’ll keep the audit read-only and avoid running tests.\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_1\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"pwd && git status --short && rg --files -g AGENTS.md -g '*yang.antlr*' -g '*datom.world.md'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_1\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"pwd && git status --short && rg --files -g AGENTS.md -g '*yang.antlr*' -g '*datom.world.md'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12\\\\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\\\\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-euV8Sa40' (errno=Operation not permitted)\\\\n2026-11-06 23:50:20.656 xcodebuild[20787:113049836]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\\\\n2026-11-06 23:50:21.048 xcodebuild[20787:113049835] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \\\\\\\"Input/output error\\\\\\\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\\\\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\\\\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-Qld1dRlb' (errno=Operation not permitted)\\\\n2026-11-06 23:50:22.535 xcodebuild[20809:113049914]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\\\\n2026-11-06 23:50:22.930 xcodebuild[20809:113049908] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \\\\\\\"Input/output error\\\\\\\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\\\\nAGENTS.md\\\\ndocs/design/datom.world.md\\\\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_2\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat AGENTS.md && cat docs/design/datom.world.md'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_2\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat AGENTS.md && cat docs/design/datom.world.md'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"# ==============================================================================\\\\n# datom.world – Development Rules & Architectural Foundations\\\\n# ==============================================================================\\\\n\\\\nSee [`docs/design/datom.world.md`](./docs/design/datom.world.md) for master architecture, core philosophy, foundational axioms, non-negotiable invariants, code style, development workflow, and operational guides (testing, team roles, agent delegation, website formats).\\\\n---\\\\ndescription: Core philosophy, foundational axioms, invariants, primitives (tuples, streams, host boundaries), architectural commitments, design principles, code style, and development workflow for datom.world\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n# DATOM.WORLD ARCHITECTURAL FOUNDATIONS & DEVELOPMENT RULES\\\\n\\\\n## Core Philosophy\\\\n\\\\nEverything is data.\\\\nInterpretation > abstraction.\\\\nExplicit causality > implicit assumptions.\\\\nRestrictions are a feature.\\\\n\\\\n### Foundational Axioms\\\\n\\\\n1. **Everything is a Stream**: Portable I/O and system data flow through append-only streams; hosts may also install explicit local functions that perform direct I/O.\\\\n2. **Interpretation Creates Semantics**: Data is syntax; semantics only emerge through interpretation (one truth, many perspectives).\\\\n   At system scale, a \\\\\\\"system\\\\\\\" is an emergent property of interpreters of\\\\n   pure data, not an object, service, or stored artifact. Find the\\\\n   interpreters and the data they share to find the system.\\\\n3. **Code and State are Datoms**: Code (Universal AST) and runtime execution state are structured datoms, enabling syntax independence and structural reflection.\\\\n4. **Everything is a Continuation**: Computation is modeled as serializable, portable continuations that can pause, travel across streams, and resume anywhere.\\\\n\\\\n## Non-Negotiable Invariants\\\\n\\\\n- Do not introduce hidden global state.\\\\n- Do not introduce implicit control flow.\\\\n- Do not introduce callbacks; every callback is an event on a stream.\\\\n- Do not introduce shared mutable state.\\\\n- Do not collapse interpretation and execution into the same layer.\\\\n- Do not assume graphs: graphs must be constructed explicitly from tuples.\\\\n- Do not lose information (unitarity): streams are append-only and no datom is destroyed, only reinterpreted. The Universal AST is never lost: it is always retrievable wherever code is lowered, by address or by a query over its datoms. Every derived form (semantic vector, native images, indexes) is an interpretation of it and may drop facts only because the AST remains.\\\\n\\\\n## Tuples and Datoms\\\\n\\\\nTuples are elements in an open moduli space, graded by dimension $n$. A tuple can be any dimension/size.\\\\nA datom is the canonical persistent tuple `[e a v t m]` (entity, attribute, value, transaction, metadata). Persistent facts are immutable datoms.\\\\nSource scope belongs to the interpreter, never to an appended tuple slot. Queries keep physical sources as separate db-values and express union or joins explicitly.\\\\n\\\\nSee [`docs/design/datom.md`](./datom.md) for full specification.\\\\n\\\\n## Streams\\\\n\\\\n`dao.stream` is an I/O monad and the system's portable I/O ABI. Functions consume streams and produce streams.\\\\nHosts may install arbitrary local functions, including direct I/O; their availability and migration semantics must be explicit.\\\\nPortable behavior cannot assume them; portable side effects appear as stream emissions. Direct-I/O host modules are explicitly local and non-migratable (owner decision, 2026-10-23).\\\\nStreams are values that can be sent through streams.\\\\nStreams carry whatever values the consumer needs: no datom requirement, no privileged payload shape.\\\\n\\\\nA stream has no privileged reader, and its meaning is not in it. Any number\\\\nof interpreters may observe the same medium, and each constructs its own\\\\nsemantics from the same batches: a `yin.vm` evaluator observing a program\\\\nstream constructs CESK state and executes it; `dao.space.index` observing\\\\nthe very same stream materializes covered indexes, so `dao.space.query/q`\\\\nanswers Datalog over the program as it grows. Neither knows the other\\\\nexists. The medium is their only coupling, and each observer's ignorance of\\\\nthe other is load-bearing: the evaluator never consults an index to run,\\\\nand the index never evaluates a form to index it. This is how axiom 2\\\\nbecomes architecture: one stream, many interpretations, none of them\\\\nthe stream's own.\\\\n\\\\nFunctions can take anything and return anything.\\\\nAgents are functions, closures, or continuations in `yin.vm` that communicate portably with the outside world through `dao.stream`. Portable agent behavior is specified through stream effects; host-local functions may also perform direct I/O.\\\\n\\\\nSee [`docs/design/dao.stream.md`](./dao.stream.md) for full stream specification.\\\\nSee [`docs/design/yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md`](./yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md) for VM architecture.\\\\n\\\\n### Host Boundaries\\\\n\\\\nA host boundary is the dao.stream abstraction boundary; implementations do not add contracts.\\\\n[datom.world.abi.md](./datom.world.abi.md) owns the doctrine, owner rulings, taxonomy, floor and custody rules.\\\\n\\\\n## Architectural Commitments\\\\n\\\\n- **`dao.jing` is syntax, agents are semantics**: the content-addressed encoding stays passive and payload-agnostic.\\\\n- **Macros are stream topology**: an evaluator knows nothing about macro expansion; expansion happens on the syntax side of a medium boundary, upstream of any evaluator.\\\\n- **Peer observers, one stream**: a generic evaluator and `dao.space` independently observe the same stream topic, as described under Streams. This is not a claim about any two consumers regardless of what they consume.\\\\n- **Observers are independent and optional**: nothing requires a medium to have any particular set of consumers. Which observers exist for a stream is a per-composition choice, not a design-time commitment.\\\\n\\\\n## Design Principles\\\\n\\\\nCode quality is measured by malleability: how cheaply can changes adapt without breaking promises?\\\\nStigmergic coordination emerges from sharing data across streams.\\\\n\\\\n**Systems emerge from interpreters of pure data.** Streams are the\\\\ncomposition medium; each interpreter gives the same data a perspective\\\\nwithout collapsing interpretation into execution or owning the truth.\\\\n\\\\n- `dao.space` emerges from `dao.space.index` and `dao.space.query` over\\\\n  ordinary streams.\\\\n- ShiBi capability, metering, and budget emerge from different\\\\n  interpreters over the same tuples; no token object is stored.\\\\n- The four VMs interpret one Universal AST; many syntaxes feed that AST.\\\\n- The semantic AST in `dao.space` is queryable facts projected by the\\\\n  auto-index observer.\\\\n- Client and server are roles in one stigmergic behavior implemented by\\\\n  interpreters, not distinct kinds of nodes.\\\\n\\\\n**Derive, don't persist.** Before adding a tag, slot, or field to any\\\\ncanonical content-hashed structure (an AST grammar, a datom schema, a row\\\\nshape), check whether a correctly scoped Datalog query over\\\\n`dao.space.query/q` can already compute the fact. If it can, it belongs as a\\\\nquery or projection: new persisted structure migrates every downstream\\\\nconsumer and duplicates authority over a fact a query derives fresh. The\\\\nretired `:global` tag in\\\\n[`docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`](./yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md) is the\\\\ncase study, including the scoping bug that a naive query introduced.\\\\n\\\\nSee [`docs/agents/malleability.md`](../agents/malleability.md) for complete design guidance (cohesion, coupling, bounded complexity, evolution, testing strategy).\\\\nSee [`docs/agents/vocabulary.md`](../agents/vocabulary.md) for domain vocabulary reference (biology, economics, physics, philosophy).\\\\n\\\\n## Code Style\\\\n\\\\n- Prefer simple data over rich types.\\\\n- Prefer total functions over partial ones.\\\\n- Prefer declarative pipelines over imperative logic.\\\\n- Avoid cleverness.\\\\n- Name things after what they do to streams.\\\\n\\\\n## Development Workflow\\\\n\\\\n- Do not invent abstractions that hide streams.\\\\n- Do not suggest mainstream frameworks unless explicitly asked.\\\\n- Do not optimize prematurely.\\\\n- When uncertain, ask at the architectural level, not the implementation level.\\\\n- Explanations should align with Plan 9 / Datomic / Lisp lineage.\\\\n- Program store writes go through `engine/store-put`; any other store write\\\\n  the store-write audit (`test/yin/vm/store_write_audit_test.clj`)\\\\n  detects must be on its allowlist; its docstring states the residual it\\\\n  leaves to review.\\\\n\\\\n### Problem Decomposition\\\\n\\\\nIf a problem appears complex:\\\\n1. Decompose it into streams.\\\\n2. Identify invariants.\\\\n3. Restrict degrees of freedom.\\\\n4. Make causality explicit.\\\\n5. Let structure emerge from constraints.\\\\n\\\\n## Operational & Specialized Guides\\\\n\\\\n- **Advanced Concepts**: See [`docs/agents/advanced-concepts.md`](../agents/advanced-concepts.md) for parallel transport, capability tokens, and entanglement.\\\\n- **Build & Test**: See [`docs/agents/build-n-test.md`](../agents/build-n-test.md) for build, lint, and test commands and TDD guidelines.\\\\n- **Engineering Team Roster**: See [`docs/agents/team.md`](../agents/team.md) for engineering team roles and LLM model assignments.\\\\n- **Agent Delegation**: See [`docs/agents/roles/orchestrator.md`](../agents/roles/orchestrator.md) for collaboration protocols and delegating tasks or reviews through `agy`, `cmd`, `glm`, `deepseek`, and `codex`; each orchestrator session has its own append-only log at `orchestrator-logs/<unix-time-stamp>-<brief-orchestrator-descriptive-name>.md` under the repository root.\\\\n- **Website & Content**: See [`docs/agents/format.md`](../agents/format.md) for `.chp` and `.blog` EDN/Hiccup file specifications.\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_3\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"rg --files | rg '(\\\\\\\"'^|/)(clojure.cljc|lower.cljc|prelude.cljc|.*(exception|conformance).*|AGENTS.md)$'\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_3\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"rg --files | rg '(\\\\\\\"'^|/)(clojure.cljc|lower.cljc|prelude.cljc|.*(exception|conformance).*|AGENTS.md)$'\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"AGENTS.md\\\\ntest/fixtures/codec/transit/exceptions.edn\\\\ntest/fixtures/codec/cbor/exceptions.edn\\\\ntest/dao/host/conformance_test.cljc\\\\ntest/dao/jing/cbor_conformance_test.cljc\\\\ntest/dao/space/datomic_query_conformance_test.cljc\\\\ntest/dao/stream/conformance.cljc\\\\ncollab/orch-lane/1793660000000-engineer-p4-yangcall-conformance.gpt-6-luna.stdout.log\\\\ncollab/orch-lane/1793810000000-engineer-p4-conformance-so-r2.gpt-6-luna.stdout.log\\\\ncollab/orch-lane/1793790000000-engineer-p4-conformance-so.gpt-6-luna.stdout.log\\\\ncollab/yang-python/1792205000000-note-to-yang-python-orchestrator-conformance.md\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\\\\ncollab/yang-call/1793610000000-orchestrator-to-ts-php-crosslang-conformance-gap.md\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/lower.cljc\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc\\\\ncollab/orchestration/1790857898202-subagent-license-gpl2-exception.claude-opus-5-5.report-r2.md\\\\ncollab/orchestration/1790857898202-subagent-license-gpl2-exception.claude-opus-5-5.stdout-r2.log\\\\ncollab/orchestration/1790857898202-subagent-license-gpl2-exception.claude-opus-5-5.report.md\\\\ncollab/orchestration/1790857898202-subagent-license-gpl2-exception.prompt.md\\\\ncollab/orchestration/1790857898202-subagent-license-gpl2-exception.claude-opus-5-5.stdout.log\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc\\\\ntools/jolt-autobahn/exceptions.json\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/core/prelude.cljc\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/core/lower.cljc\\\\ntest/yang/call/conformance.clj\\\\ncollab/yin-vm-wasm/retired-2026-10-19-yin.vm.conformance-kit.md\\\\ntest/yang/antlr/conformance.cljc\\\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/exceptions_test.clj\\\\ncollab/general/1790858923272-reviewer-license-gpl2-exception-gate.gpt-6.1-sol.findings-r2.md\\\\ncollab/general/1790858923272-reviewer-license-gpl2-exception-gate.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md\\\\ncollab/general/1790858923272-reviewer-license-gpl2-exception-gate.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\\\\ncollab/general/1790858923272-reviewer-license-gpl2-exception-gate.prompt.md\\\\ncollab/general/1790858923272-reviewer-license-gpl2-exception-gate.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout-r2.log\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_4\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '3810,3930p' docs/design/yang.antlr.md; sed -n '4040,4135p' docs/design/yang.antlr.md; rg -n 'raise|thrown|ForeignException|exception|catch|finally|run-main' src/yang/clojure.cljc src/yang/{typescript,php,python}/antlr/{lower,prelude}.cljc\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_4\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '3810,3930p' docs/design/yang.antlr.md; sed -n '4040,4135p' docs/design/yang.antlr.md; rg -n 'raise|thrown|ForeignException|exception|catch|finally|run-main' src/yang/clojure.cljc src/yang/{typescript,php,python}/antlr/{lower,prelude}.cljc\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"arbitrary foreign arithmetic or object access is not implied. Every\\\\nadvertised projection needs separate behavioral conformance tests.\\\\n\\\\n#### 8.10.6 References, higher-order calls, and ownership\\\\n\\\\nBy-value arguments may contain shared object references. That does not\\\\nauthorize rebinding the caller's variable: a value read from a local is\\\\nnot a location capability.\\\\n\\\\nSource-local reference arguments keep their pinned native binding\\\\nprofile. A call requiring foreign writable locations must declare a\\\\ncompatible profile or fail with a guest binding error before the body.\\\\nSilently allocating a temporary and claiming writeback is forbidden.\\\\nA location extension must define read/write operations, alias identity,\\\\nevaluation of nested paths exactly once, lifetime, ownership, cleanup,\\\\nand suspension. Generic callers must not decode PHP reference markers\\\\nor bypass its copy/count rules.\\\\n\\\\nFunctions passed, returned, or called recursively keep the common entry\\\\nand original identity. This includes calls back into a runtime already\\\\non the stack. No caller-side rewrapping or language-pair cache is allowed.\\\\n\\\\nThese are in-task rules. A closure, continuation, cell, or live invocation\\\\nis not made portable by this convention. Linker/UCF custody and admission\\\\nstill govern task/host crossings; currently refused cell-bearing lifts\\\\nremain refused. Live closures in an invocation must not be placed in\\\\ncanonical literal data or sent as a purported portable request.\\\\n\\\\n#### 8.10.7 Normal return and escaping conditions\\\\n\\\\nNormal return is the value of ordinary Yin application. There is no\\\\nextra return continuation, completion packet around each result, or new\\\\nlanguage-specific return instruction.\\\\n\\\\nAn escaping source exception invokes the supplied raise exit with:\\\\n\\\\n```clojure\\\\n{:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown\\\\n :yang.call/value  original-thrown-value}\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nThis is the argument to an exceptional continuation transfer, not an\\\\nordinary return. Returning an identical-looking map returns normal data.\\\\nLikewise, a source program throwing a map with these keys throws that\\\\nmap as the **payload of a new condition**; its shape is never evidence\\\\nthat it is already a condition to forward. No engine-effect value is\\\\nsynthesized.\\\\n\\\\nProtocol failures use qualified reasons such as\\\\n`:yang.call/not-callable`, `:yang.call/invalid-invocation`, and\\\\n`:yang.call/unsupported-binding`, with plain evidence. The caller maps\\\\nthem to a documented local exception form retaining the complete\\\\noriginal condition. Callee argument-binding failures retain the actual\\\\ncallee exception under `:yang.call/thrown`. These reasons do not extend\\\\n`dao.stream`'s outcome algebra.\\\\n\\\\nThe receiving caller interprets an escaping exception as follows:\\\\n\\\\n1. A payload valid as an exception in its own runtime retains that\\\\n   runtime's ordinary catching and identity behavior.\\\\n2. A runtime permitting arbitrary thrown values, such as JavaScript,\\\\n   may deliver the original payload directly.\\\\n3. A runtime requiring exception objects, such as Python or PHP,\\\\n   represents an otherwise foreign payload with its own\\\\n   `ForeignException`, retaining the complete condition and original\\\\n   payload. Catch-all catches this local object. Typed source catches\\\\n   match its local hierarchy, never guessed foreign class names.\\\\n\\\\n`ForeignException` is a proposed prelude-owned type, not a VM type.\\\\nUnchanged rethrow propagates the original condition without adding\\\\nwrappers. Raising a new exception creates a new condition. Crossing back\\\\ninto a runtime recognizing the original exception restores its original\\\\ntype and identity. Formatting a foreign payload must not implicitly\\\\ninvoke a foreign method.\\\\n\\\\nThe runtime associates its generated wrapper's identity with the retained\\\\ncondition for the wrapper's entire lifetime, separate from source-writable\\\\nattributes. The association normally lives in private wrapper-cell\\\\ncontents, or an equivalent task-owned identity structure with the same\\\\nlifetime. It survives storing or returning the wrapper after the creating\\\\ncall/catch activation has ended, and remains recoverable when that same\\\\nwrapper is rethrown in another activation. Temporary catch state alone is\\\\ninsufficient. Reachability/reclamation must retain the condition and its\\\\npayload while the wrapper is live, without an ambient registry.\\\\n\\\\nThe runtime must not detect wrappers or unwrap arbitrary maps by their\\\\nkey names. JavaScript may expose raw payloads for\\\\n`:yang.call/thrown`; its local exception for a protocol failure must still\\\\nretain that failure's qualified condition. Rethrowing the same generated\\\\nexception forwards that complete condition, including protocol reasons;\\\\nthrowing an unrelated value creates a new `:yang.call/thrown` condition.\\\\nSaved activation state refers to this identity-owned association; exiting\\\\nor restoring a catch does not destroy it.\\\\n\\\\nVM application/custody defects and host implementation failures remain\\\\noperational failures. Do not catch them broadly and relabel them as\\\\nsource exceptions. Existing explicit stream/module refusals keep their\\\\nsource mappings under the relevant profiles.\\\\n\\\\n#### 8.10.8 Cleanup, re-entry, and suspension\\\\n\\\\nEach activation establishes its own exception bridge and saves its\\\\ncallee runtime's dynamic context. Binding, body, and exit run under that\\\\nbridge. Before invoking the caller's raise exit, let source catches and\\\\ncleanup complete and restore saved handler/depth/frame state. Normal\\\\nreturn restores it too. A source `finally` replacing a pending return\\\\nor exception does so before common propagation under its own rules.\\\\n\\\\nIn A-to-B-to-A calls, the innermost activation must not jump to an older\\\\nA handler past B. Its entry bridge is the boundary: inner A cleanup\\\\nprecedes B cleanup, which precedes outer A handling. Every activation\\\\nowns its saved state and raise exit, without a single current-foreign-\\\\nhandler cell or ambient dispatcher. Unchanged rethrow preserves the\\\\ninner exception as specified in section 8.10.7.\\\\n\\\\nCleanup runs once per actual exit. Resuming a suspended VM transition\\\\nmust not repeat parameter binding, argument evaluation, defaults,\\\\nreference acquisition, or completed cleanup. The record, continuations,\\\\nand explicit runtime state use the existing continuation machinery and\\\\nits admission restrictions.\\\\n\\\\n- **Presence and binding:** distinguish missing from explicit\\\\n  null/None/undefined; retain duplicate keywords until binding; supply\\\\n  bound self once; evaluate receiver/spreads/defaults at source-defined\\\\n  times and counts.\\\\n- **Dynamic callability:** where supported, an existing instance becomes\\\\n  eligible after its class gains a call method and ineligible after\\\\n  deletion. Calls whose arguments change this metadata observe the\\\\n  correct source-required lookup time without instance rewrapping.\\\\n- **Opaque values:** round-trip foreign objects, functions, strings,\\\\n  float64 content, and exact integers unchanged. Assert aliasing and no\\\\n  silent rounding/null conversion. Unsupported operations yield\\\\n  documented guest errors.\\\\n- **References:** absent/incompatible writable-location profiles fail\\\\n  before reference acquisition and the body, with no reference-induced\\\\n  writeback. Source-required side effects from evaluating arguments still\\\\n  occur; rejection must not erase them. Compatible profiles prove\\\\n  mutation, aliasing, cleanup, and suspension behavior.\\\\n- **Exceptions:** cover binding failures, arbitrary foreign thrown data,\\\\n  catch-all/typed catches, unchanged rethrow, replacement in `finally`,\\\\n  protocol-error rethrow, condition-shaped thrown maps, and A-to-B-to-A\\\\n  propagation. Assert original exception identity and cleanup order,\\\\n  not only rendered text. Store/return a generated `ForeignException`,\\\\n  finish its creating activation, then rethrow it from another activation\\\\n  and assert recovery of the original condition and payload identity.\\\\n- **Context lifetime:** repeated success/raise/success, cross-runtime\\\\n  recursion, and stream suspension/resume restore handler/depth/frame\\\\n  state and perform arguments/cleanup exactly once. Entry boilerplate\\\\n  must not double-count source recursion or tracing activations.\\\\n- **Publication/custody:** bundled/linked forms agree; two importing\\\\n  tasks have independent state. Existing gates still refuse foreign-task\\\\n  cells, forged refs, host functions, and inadmissible continuations.\\\\n- **Portability:** execute portable packet-to-UAST fixtures on JVM,\\\\n  Node, and Dart over the four VMs wherever existing contracts admit\\\\n  the program. JVM-only parsers may supply checked-in CST fixtures;\\\\n  parser availability is distinct from calling conformance.\\\\n\\\\nReport callable kinds, binding/value extensions, actual host/VM\\\\ncoverage as an explicit host-by-VM matrix, refusals, and remaining gaps\\\\nper frontend revision. A scalar example or common UAST grammar alone\\\\ndoes not establish conformance.\\\\n\\\\n#### 8.10.12 Cell-reference call routing and authenticity\\\\n\\\\nRuling of record (2026-11-04, owner-approved). A cross-language\\\\nreference is a cell-ref map the VM issues (`{:type :cell-ref :id\\\\n:cell-N :seal s}`). In Clojure a map is callable, so the call lowering\\\\nmust route a callee between reference semantics and data semantics.\\\\nThree rounds routed by value shape at call time (key presence,\\\\nexact shape, minted-id language) and each left the same defect class:\\\\ninnocent data whose shape imitates the reference language aborted at\\\\n`cell/get` instead of answering as data. The defect is structural — a\\\\ngenuine reference and a perfect imitation are field-identical maps,\\\\nand the distinguishing fact (did the heap issue this?) is not in the\\\\nvalue. It is in the heap. Only the issuer can answer.\\\\n\\\\n- **Vocabulary.** The `cell` host module's published effect vocabulary\\\\n  is `{new, get, set!, authentic?}`. `cell/authentic?` is a pure\\\\n  query: the engine answers the same heap+seal predicate `check-ref!`\\\\n  consults, as a boolean, non-fatally, state unchanged. The engine\\\\n  learns no frontend semantics; it answers a generic fact about its\\\\n  own state (the no-collapse invariant holds — the invoke-vs-lookup\\\\n  decision remains in compiled guest code).\\\\n- **Routing asks the heap, never the shape.** Where the callee value\\\\n  has the cell-ref shape, compiled code consults `cell/authentic?`:\\\\n  authentic → the reference path (`cell/get` plus the existing\\\\n  admission/apply machinery); not authentic → ordinary data semantics\\\\n  (map lookup). The shape remains a cheap pre-filter for WHEN to ask;\\\\n  it never decides meaning. The shared descriptor projection\\\\n  (`yang.call/_descriptor`) consults the same way.\\\\n- **Interim asymmetry (agreed across the four seats).** The frontend\\\\n  kind predicates that route on a `:type :cell-ref` tag before\\\\n  dereferencing — TypeScript's `js/cell?` and Python's `py/cell?` —\\\\n  still test SHAPE alone at this landing; their owning seats sweep\\\\n  them onto `cell/authentic?` in-lane after this merge (TypeScript:\\\\n  the `typeof` path and member-call lowering; Python: the three deref\\\\n  sites — `py/content-type`, type resolution, `py/eq-objects`). Until\\\\n  those sweeps land, a map imitating the reference language is data\\\\n  at Clojure positions and at the shared descriptor projection, but\\\\n  can still abort at the unswept frontend predicates. Nothing\\\\n  currently-correct changes behavior (the widening property holds);\\\\n  all-frontends consistency completes at the owning seats' landings.\\\\n- **Authentication is not authorization.** An authentic reference\\\\n  whose cell lacks an admitted callable entry is not callable; the\\\\n  existing not-callable refusal stands. Explicit dereference at a\\\\n  reference position (`cell/get`) likewise keeps the strict\\\\n  validation boundary — the data fallback lives in call routing.\\\\n- **Bearer policy.** An exact copy of a valid reference retains\\\\n  bearer behavior: it authenticates, therefore it resolves. No\\\\n  construction-history promises are made for identical values. A\\\\n  program wanting such a map's fields as data uses explicit lookup at\\\\n  a data position.\\\\n- **Bag clarification.** A reference stored in data remains a\\\\n  reference: storage changes nothing about the value, and what\\\\n  decides is the authentication query at the eventual call, not where\\\\n  the callee travelled. Equality survives while callability follows\\\\n  the heap's answer.\\\\nrg: src/yang/clojure.cljc: No such file or directory (os error 2)\\\\nrg: src/yang/typescript/antlr/lower.cljc: No such file or directory (os error 2)\\\\nrg: src/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc: No such file or directory (os error 2)\\\\nrg: src/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc: No such file or directory (os error 2)\\\\nrg: src/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc: No such file or directory (os error 2)\\\\nrg: src/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc: No such file or directory (os error 2)\\\\nrg: src/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc: No such file or directory (os error 2)\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":2,\\\"status\\\":\\\"failed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\