uential?, from the `portable/*` adapters of data/count,\\\\n  2420\\\\t;; peek, dissoc and disj: a refusal as data says \\\\\\\"not that kind\\\\\\\"), boolean?,\\\\n  2421\\\\t;; fn? (data/callable?), seq, rem, reverse, list, cons, vector, count,\\\\n  2422\\\\t;; contains?, rest, map/mapv/filter/remove/reduce (with reduced)/into/concat/merge,\\\\n  2423\\\\t;; keys/vals/disj and set union/difference,\\\\n  2424\\\\t;; comp, partial, gensym (explicit supply), not=, and `apply`, which is a\\\\n  2425\\\\t;; compiler intrinsic over the convention's argument vector.\\\\n  2426\\\\t;;\\\\n  2427\\\\t;; What stays a host primitive, named by the `kind` module: a symbol, a\\\\n  2428\\\\t;; keyword and a host string are distinguished or built only by the host\\\\n  2429\\\\t;; (symbol?, keyword?, name, symbol, keyword, str, int?), as is metadata access\\\\n  2430\\\\t;; (meta and with-meta). The current data ABI has no metadata-write export,\\\\n  2431\\\\t;; so with-meta is an explicit pure representation seam, not an ambient store.\\\\n  2432\\\\t;; No VM primitive tells a symbol from a keyword. Clojure Var identity is an\\\\n  2433\\\\t;; explicitly admitted kind/var? seam on the JVM; namespace lookup (resolve)\\\\n  2434\\\\t;; still requires a separately installed host capability.\\\\n  2435\\\\t;;\\\\n  2436\\\\t;; Known compromises: `reduced` is an untyped tagged map, so reduced? matches\\\\n  2437\\\\t;; any map holding :yin.k/reduced true; seq refuses a non-collection (a string\\\\n  2438\\\\t;; is the data module's str-* ops, not a seq); eager sequences are lists;\\\\n  2439\\\\t;; rem rejects non-integers and a zero divisor before arithmetic; the compiler\\\\n  2440\\\\t;; emits bare conj and vec, so a program may not define or bind either.\\\\n  2441\\\\t;; When collection calls are needed, invoke-value is a library helper whose\\\\n  2442\\\\t;; local capture is refused explicitly.\\\\n  2443\\\\t;;\\\\n  2444\\\\t;; Variadic Clojure functions are fixed-arity