           (u/lit :clj/outcomes?) (u/lit true))\\\\n  1161\\\\t    tail?))\\\\n  1162\\\\t\\\\n  1163\\\\t\\\\n  1164\\\\t(defn- compile-av-fn\\\\n  1165\\\\t  \\\\\\\"Compile arities [{:params :body}] to one closure over an argument vector.\\\\n  1238\\\\t  [env operator]\\\\n  1239\\\\t  (and (outcomes? env)\\\\n  1240\\\\t       (symbol? operator)\\\\n  1241\\\\t       (not (contains? (locals env) operator))\\\\n  1242\\\\t       (contains? (::defined-fns env) operator)))\\\\n  1243\\\\t\\\\n  1244\\\\t\\\\n  1245\\\\t(defn- cell-ref-shaped-node\\\\n  1246\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The UAST test that the callee node could be a cell reference the\\\\n  1247\\\\t   VM issued: `:type :cell-ref` with the `:id` and `:seal` every\\\\n  1248\\\\t   issued reference carries, no other entries, a seal of the issued\\\\n  1249\\\\t   form (a 64-character string), and an `:id` in the engine's heap\\\\n  1250\\\\t   id language — every cell id is a `:cell-N` keyword (engine\\\\n  1251\\\\t   `gen-id` mints them all from one counter), so an `:id` that is\\\\n  1252\\\\t   not such a keyword names no cell the task could ever have\\\\n  1253\\\\t   minted and the map is data, whatever its other entries spell.\\\\n  1254\\\\t   A map that fails this test is never dereferenced: it routes to\\\\n  1255\\\\t   ordinary map invocation, which grants no cell capability. A map\\\\n  1256\\\\t   that passes it is a dereference *candidate*, not a proven\\\\n  1257\\\\t   reference — authenticity is the VM's heap+seal check at the\\\\n  1258\\\\t   dereference, which this frontend cannot observe (a failed\\\\n  1259\\\\t   check is a host-level refusal, outside every guest catch), so\\\\n  1260\\\\t   the candidate is offered to admission and the VM governs:\\\\n  1261\\\\t   genuine references dereference to their cell's entry, and a\\\\n  1262\\\\t   forged candidate fails closed in the VM exactly as any forged\\\\n  1263\\\\t   reference must.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  1264\\\\t  [callee]\\\\n  1265\\\\t  (let