{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"agent_message","text":"The code supports keeping v2. Clojure has explicit depth-regression tests for its private outcome path; the continuation preludes perform restoration after the body returns, so copying that pattern would introduce work after calls that are currently tail calls. The preludes also differ in context restoration and normal-return behavior, so any shared core needs explicit parameters. I’ll distinguish that optional refactor from the mandatory R4 equivalence proof.\n"}}
