{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-11-10 19:22:34 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-11 02:22:34 ICT\n\n**Ruling: (A) Keep v2 as-is.** Enforce boundary uniformity; retain Clojure’s internal outcomes only upon satisfying R4’s equivalence requirement. V2 expressly permits different internal lowering and makes outcome retention conditional, not grandfathered. [v2:22–30](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/exception-track/1794960000000-owner-ruling-exception-uniformity-v2.md:22), [v2:69–75](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/exception-track/1794960000000-owner-ruling-exception-uniformity-v2.md:69).\n\n**Dominant tradeoff:** preserving Clojure’s bounded tail depth, subject to proof, is preferable to accepting B’s restoration-related depth cost or imposing C’s outcome-return protocol and rewrite cost on three additional frontends. The existing depth gates and outcome propagation machinery substantiate those concerns. [clojure_test.clj:1584–1618](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/clojure_test.clj:1584), [clojure.cljc:840–864](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:840), [clojure.cljc:1026–1061](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1026).\n\nMy reasoning is:\n\n1. **The common contract already specifies the observable distinction that matters.** Normal application returns its value; an escaping exception transfers to the supplied raise exit. A returned condition-shaped map remains data, and throwing one creates a fresh condition containing that map. Internal tuples must disappear at public boundaries. [yang.antlr.md:3838–3864](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yang.antlr.md:3838). Clojure already has a public outcome-to-value/raise adapter and `%capture` bridges; it is not an alternative VM exception mechanism. [clojure.cljc:1283–1312](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1283), [clojure.cljc:1506–1562](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1506). The canonical grammar contains continuation operations but no exception-specific nodes. [vm.cljc:997–1018](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:997).\n\n2. **B’s stated tail-depth regression is unacceptable merely to obtain implementation uniformity.** Clojure’s private entry forwards outcomes in tail position; its tests explicitly compare self and mutual-call depths at 100 and 1,000 iterations, with a non-tail negative control. These are test obligations, not a claim that I reran them. [clojure.cljc:1313–1355](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1313), [clojure_test.clj:1584–1618](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/clojure_test.clj:1584).\n\n   The relevant cost is **pending restoration after a call**, not `%capture` intrinsically. For example, `js/try` restores context after `(body)` returns; the semantic VM retains a return frame for non-tail closure calls. Copying that activation pattern into recursive Clojure calls therefore threatens the existing depth property. [TypeScript prelude:1725–1735](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc:1725), [semantic.cljc:190–199](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:190). This does not prove that every possible continuation implementation must lose constant depth.\n\n3. **C’s costs are also unjustified by this track’s objective.** Outcome lowering changes successful returns and threads failure checks through operands while preserving evaluation order; adopting it elsewhere is a compiler/runtime transformation, not replacing the spelling of `throw`. [clojure.cljc:840–864](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:840), [clojure.cljc:1026–1061](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1026). The three continuation runtimes already express finalization and nonlocal exits through their handler machinery. [Python prelude:329–351](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:329), [TypeScript prelude:1736–1756](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc:1736), [PHP prelude:272–296](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:272). I would not authorize that rewrite without a demonstrated benefit beyond identical internal representation.\n\nThe concrete follow-up work is:\n\n1. **Complete the existing repair rounds in v2’s order.** JS R1/R3; PHP R1/R2/R3 together; Python R2/R3 including egress; Clojure R3 before R4. This ruling does not postpone provenance repairs. [v2:118–132](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/exception-track/1794960000000-owner-ruling-exception-uniformity-v2.md:118). Preserve the distinction between authenticated retained conditions and freshly thrown maps, including the prior value-path ruling; internal unification would not eliminate that distinction. [prior provenance finding:71–81](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/exception-track/1794320926000-architect-dsg-condition-r4-coupling.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:71), [prior value-path ruling:1566–1583](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/exception-track/1794332020000-architect-value-path-refusal-shape.codex-astra.stdout.log:1566).\n\n2. **Make R4 a separate proof-and-regression round.** Compare authenticated private calls with public-entry calls for caught/uncaught throws, binding failures, protocol rethrow, and higher-order re-entry. Extend observations to evaluation order, effects, suspension, identity, delayed rethrow, and separately compiled units. Include returned/thrown outcome-shaped values and forged provenance markers. Preserve the depth gates and recompute tail marks after wrapping transformations. These implement R4 and §8.10.9’s broader equivalence bar. [v2:69–79](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/exception-track/1794960000000-owner-ruling-exception-uniformity-v2.md:69), [yang.antlr.md:3970–3975](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yang.antlr.md:3970), [tails.cljc:1–6](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/tails.cljc:1). **Failure leaves R4 open; it does not earn an exception to conformance.**\n\n3. **Finish the existing 12-direction acceptance matrix.** This is already required, not newly justified work. Include callable kinds, identity before rendering, cleanup order, A→B→A, retained-wrapper lifetime, suspension, and admitted host/VM paths. A green pair matrix cannot substitute for private/public equivalence—the fixture contract explicitly separates them. [v2:89–116](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/exception-track/1794960000000-owner-ruling-exception-uniformity-v2.md:89), [exception_contract.clj:143–177](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/call/exception_contract.clj:143).\n\n4. **Permit a separate, optional shared-prelude extraction after semantic repair.** Factor the repeated capture/handler/finalizer skeleton through a compile-time generator, parameterized by runtime symbols, context save/restore operations, frame operations, normal-exit behavior, and sentinel values. Keep context cells task/runtime-owned. Parameters are necessary: Python preserves the current `:base` during restoration, while JS restores the saved record; Python/PHP `try` invoke `orelse`, while JS preserves the body result. [Python prelude:275–328](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:275), [TypeScript prelude:1690–1735](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc:1690), [PHP prelude:258–271](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:258). Require differential behavior checks before replacing the copies. This refactor is not an additional exception-track completion gate.\n\nNo new owner decision is needed to retain the approved scope. Accepting a tail-depth regression or expanding Clojure’s catch/finally surface should return as a separate owner decision; v2 explicitly leaves that source-semantics restriction unchanged. [v2:69–75](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/exception-track/1794960000000-owner-ruling-exception-uniformity-v2.md:69).\n\nStatic adjudication only. No implementation changes or tests run."}}
